---
/**
 * Home section head (plan 3.3 label grammar, 4.4 #8):
 * a strong hairline that draws (scaleX) + "[ 02 ] SELECTED WORK" in the margin
 * column + the H2 in the copy column. The block fades once on entry.
 */
interface Props {
  n: string;
  label: string;
  id: string;
  /** right-aligned mono aside, e.g. "Updated Oct 2026" */
  aside?: string;
  /** Label-only head: the H2 stays for the outline but is visually hidden,
      so the section's own content carries the display type (varies the rhythm). */
  quiet?: boolean;
}
const { n, label, id, aside, quiet = false } = Astro.props;
---

<div class:list={['sh grid', { 'sh--quiet': quiet }]} data-reveal>
  <span class="sh__rule reveal-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <p class="col-label t-label sh__label"><span class="label-index">[ {n} ]</span> {label}</p>
  {
    quiet ? (
      <h2 id={id} class="sr-only"><slot /></h2>
    ) : (
      <div class="col-copy sh__copy">
        <h2 id={id} class="sh__h"><slot /></h2>
        {Astro.slots.has('intro') && <div class="sh__intro c-ink-2"><slot name="intro" /></div>}
      </div>
    )
  }
  {aside && <p class="sh__aside t-label">{aside}</p>}
</div>

<style>
  .sh {
    position: relative;
    padding-top: var(--sp-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-7);
    row-gap: var(--sp-4);
  }
  .sh__rule {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .sh__label { padding-top: .35em; }
  .sh--quiet { margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); }
  .sh__intro { margin-top: var(--sp-4); max-width: 46ch; }
  .sh__aside { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .sh__aside { grid-column: 11 / -1; text-align: right; padding-top: .35em; grid-row: 1; }
  }
</style>
